{"agent": "builder", "box": "C2", "stage": "build", "cwd": "p3-C2", "kind": "start", "cmd": "sh -c git add assets_pipeline/a4_mdl_convert.py assets_pipeline/mdl_scene.py assets_pipeline/importer.py tests/test_a4_mesh.py && git commit -q -F - <<\"EOF\"\nC2: export each loaded A-4 station as its own mesh (manifest v4 components)\n\nMdlScene.added_parts diffs parts(REST+station vars) against parts(REST)\nby Part.index. a4_mdl_convert factors _filter_part/_write_obj out of\nconvert() (body.obj byte-identical: sha 6a60a618..., 266,886 tris) and\nwrites SM_A4_<component id>.obj/.mtl per payload component of\nlabels.components, one station at a time (STA2 5,676 / STA3 5,612 /\nSTA4 5,676 triangles, the measured deltas of decision 2). The manifest\nis version 4 with components[] rows (id, class, station, part,\nasset_path, triangles, actor-frame mesh_extent_actor_m,\nmesh_origin_actor_cm = the body origin, mass_lb); gear gets no row.\nimporter.stale_manifest_reason sends a manifest whose config states a\nloading.loadout back through the converter when it is below version 4\nor has no components (other airframes stay on version 3).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TYf9hdwcEyKovqfAJKwdzh\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git status --short", "note": "commit C2 on p3-C2 (named files only; .scratch stays untracked)", "t": 1793814298.399447, "machine": "mac"}
